Looking at this problem, I need to analyze the eigenspace $E_1 = \ker(I - R)$ for the Gaussian Markov operator $R$ on $L_1(\mathbb{R}, \mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R}), Q)$ with $Q = N(\nu, \tau^2)$.

**Answer-leak check:** The problem text contains no solutions, proof sketches, or answer values. Proceeding.

